<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Noshout</h1>
<p>A player who is noshouted has "a sore throat": they can't <a cmd='#'>shout</a> until 
it wears off. Their channels, says and tells still work.
</p><p>You get noshouted:
</p>
<ul><li>automatically, for one hour, when you use a swear word in a shout;</li>
<li>by an immortal, for half an hour or as long as they choose, for spamming or abusing shout. A New Player Guide can do the same to players of level 20 or below.</li></ul>
<p>Type <a cmd='#'>noshouted</a> to see how long you have done, and wait it out: don't 
mail the admin who noshouted you begging to be let off, which may only 
make it longer. Keep the public channels friendly (see <a cmd='#'>Help Rules</a>).
</p><p>For immortals and guides:
</p>
<pre>noshout &lt;player&gt;                  for 30 minutes
noshout &lt;player&gt; 25 min           for as long as you say
noshout &lt;player&gt; 1 hour
noshout &lt;player&gt;                  (again) lifts it
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Shout</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Comm</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Rules</a>
</pre>




</div>